Subject: Check unknown container fields without calling IsNil on scalars

The ytypes container validator used by management-common can encounter an
unknown scalar field. Calling reflect.IsNil on it panics. Use the existing
nil-or-default predicate so unset/default fields remain harmless and
non-default unknown fields still reach the existing rejection checks.
Preserve choice handling and SONiC's readonly-field behavior.

Origin: SONiC shared-module correction covered by the original container
tests and overlay/ytypes/sonic_container_defaults_test.go.
https://github.com/securely1g/sonic-bazel-registry/pull/214

diff --git a/ytypes/container.go b/ytypes/container.go
--- a/ytypes/container.go
+++ b/ytypes/container.go
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
 						errors = util.AppendErrs(errors, errs)
 					}
 				}
-			case !structElems.Field(i).IsNil():
+			case !util.IsValueNilOrDefault(fieldValue):
 				// Either an element in choice schema subtree, or bad field.
 				// If the former, it will be found in the choice check below.
 				extraFields[fieldName] = nil
